  "term": "myoclonus",
  "definition": "Myoclonus is a sudden, involuntary, shock-like jerking of one muscle or a group of muscles, with irregular timing and strength, followed by relaxation. It can occur as a feature of some central nervous system disorders, including myoclonic epilepsy.",
